# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated experiment-loop views.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ledger.md is rebuilt byte-for-byte by `packing-ledger render` and drift-checked by
# `packing-ledger check` through `packing-validate`. Formatting it makes the
# check fail forever: flowmark rewraps the generated text, ledger.py regenerates
# the unwrapped form, and the two never agree. Measured on 2026-08-22 -- the gate
# failed on the first run after the file was formatted.
packing/campaign/ledger.md

# defects.md is the same case, and was missed when the rule above was written: it is
# rebuilt by `devtools.render_defects` and drift-checked through `packing-validate`.
# flowmark reflows it today -- verified on 2026-08-23 against
# main, where `flowmark --check` reports it would reformat. Any commit touching
# Markdown on a machine with the lefthook pre-commit hook installed would have
# reformatted it and left the gate failing until someone regenerated it.
#
# The gate now enforces this list rather than trusting it: `packing-validate` fails if a file
# carrying the generated-by banner is not named here.
defects.md

# STATUS.md is the complete reader view generated from the validated case and evidence
# records by devtools.render_research_tables. `packing-validate` compares it byte-for-byte
# with a fresh render; allowing Flowmark to rewrite its 100-row table would create two
# competing owners for the same file.
packing/frontier/STATUS.md

# INVENTORY.md is generated from the evidence register by
# devtools.render_evidence_inventory and drift-checked byte-for-byte in
# `packing-validate --records`. Same case as STATUS.md: two owners for one file.
packing/frontier/INVENTORY.md

# RESULTS.md is generated from the results register by devtools.render_results
# and drift-checked byte-for-byte in `packing-validate --records`. Same case as
# STATUS.md: two owners for one file.
packing/frontier/RESULTS.md

# agenda-map.md is rebuilt by `devtools.render_agenda_map` from every agenda's
# frontmatter and drift-checked in `packing-validate --records`. Same case as
# ledger.md and defects.md: two owners for one file means the check never passes.
packing/campaign/agenda-map.md

# CERTIFICATE-REACH.md is generated from the frontier case files and the certificate
# module's own ceiling by devtools.render_certificate_reach, drift-checked in
# `packing-validate --records`. Same case as RESULTS.md: two owners for one file.
packing/frontier/CERTIFICATE-REACH.md

# The verifiable-claim documents are generated by devtools.render_verifiable_claim
# from one template, the claim verifier and the certificate each embeds, and
# drift-checked byte-for-byte in tests/test_verify_claim.py. Same case as
# RESULTS.md: two owners for one file.
packing/cases/n11_fractional_certificate/t-018-verifiable-claim-19-5.md
packing/cases/n11_fractional_certificate/t-018-verifiable-claim-381-100.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two dated reviews whose quoted sources the formatter rewrites.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Measured on 2026-09-05 with the pinned flowmark-rs in directory mode (the hook's
# mode; single-file mode leaves both untouched): 9 lines change in the first and 7 in
# the second, 3 and 6 of them inside block quotes of external sources -- straight
# quotes retyped as curly inside material this repository never retypes -- and one
# genuine corruption, a quoted line beginning ">= 0" read as a block-quote marker and
# rewritten "> = 0". A dated review is an immutable determination and its quotations
# are evidence, so the two stay raw. The drift had every commit's hook re-staging
# them; eight sub-agent worktrees reverted it by hand on 2026-09-05 (think-thto).
docs/project/reviews/review-2026-09-03-bc152-h060-prior-art-survey.md
docs/project/reviews/review-2026-09-03-bc158-h060-record-factual-review.md

